ail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I77a81a86b5fc1fceae8987a3c3e19ede639f57a1" commit="5ebcacf43242378e88d05bc64d880335d9badb28" commit_message="factory_netboot: Change build target name to factory_netboot.  The chromeos-initramfs now builds factory netboot folder with name 'factory_netboot' so we should stop overriding the target name.  BUG=chromium:477744 TEST=make; build_packages; build_image; make_netboot.sh CQ-DEPEND=CL:368110,CL:368120  Change-Id: I77a81a86b5fc1fceae8987a3c3e19ede639f57a1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/368051 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="368051" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/initramfs" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/initramfs" ref="refs/changes/51/368051/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia423d859f40e100b83ef6d15c3720f9b3bba41d4" commit="29207a0a2e0e3120ab233f33b8f1861a3d0efcf8" commit_message="chromeos-initramfs: Change 'netboot_ramfs' to right name 'factory_netboot_ramfs'.  The 'netboot_ramfs' was actually referring to 'factory netboot' in initramfs folder and should be renamed to be consistent.  The build rules are also simplified due to the new consistent names.  BUG=chromium:477744 TEST=build_packages; build_image; ./make_netboot.sh CQ-DEPEND=CL:368051,CL:368120  Change-Id: Ia423d859f40e100b83ef6d15c3720f9b3bba41d4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/368110 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="368110" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/10/368110/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If02cc0990a102479854b08000255dd8acd3f83ce" commit="ae6bc859739da7168a024bd174c20bb7b8bdc8d3" commit_message="make_netboot: Change use flags to right name 'factory_netboot_ramfs'.  In CL:368110 the netboot_ramfs USE flag is changed to factory_netboot_ramfs, and the netboot builder script should use the new name.  BUG=chromium:477744 TEST=./make_netboot.sh CQ-DEPEND=CL:368110,CL:368051  Change-Id: If02cc0990a102479854b08000255dd8acd3f83ce Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/368120 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="368120" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/crosutils" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/crosutils" ref="refs/changes/20/368120/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I205bbd4f03e737281f3d27c790cea076205818e6" commit="70db78dadfce1020c4cf8e77886bc49dffff8a3d" commit_message="cryptohome: Extract attestation into dbus service child class  To prepare for implementing a version of cryptohome dbus service that bounces attestation-related calls to attestationd, extract attestation-related functionality into a separate class dependant on Service and make attestation-related methods abstract in the base Service.  This approach was chosen over extracting it into a separate class that can be instantiated by Service depending on the chosen attestation implementation for the following reasons: To minimize changes to the existing code, attestation methods continue to rely on Service's internal objects: mount_thread, event_source, etc. They also occasionally use tpm, tpm_init and other such objects, pointers to which are handled by Service. Giving access to it for dependant classes is more natural and less intrusive than exposing all needed internal objects to an independant class. Thus, after the two approaches (inheritance vs object encapsulation) were implemented and compared, inheritance had a more concise code and required less changes to the code that uses Service: interface, cryptohomed, unittests.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54712 TEST=cryptohome unittests      cryptohome --action=tpm_attestation_status      cryptohome --action=tpm_more_status      login_Cryptohome      platform_Attestation (TPM1.2 only)  Change-Id: I205bbd4f03e737281f3d27c790cea076205818e6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/368890 Commit-Ready: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="368890" owner_email="apronin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/90/368890/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I43ebc6a184ba07cc2f787d6a788a92f6fa7153a6" commit="bafb391960b5eb82473190b771854e0d1116b9e1" commit_message="cryptohome: add empty skeleton for ServiceDistributed  Add ServiceDistributed class inherited from Service that will forward attestation-related tasks to attestationd instead of processing them locally. Create empty skeleton implementation.  Use ServiceDistributed by default for TPM2.0 case.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54712 TEST=cryptohome unittests      cryptohome --action=tpm_attestation_status      cryptohome --action=tpm_more_status      login_Cryptohome      platform_Attestation (TPM1.2 only)  Change-Id: I43ebc6a184ba07cc2f787d6a788a92f6fa7153a6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/368891 Commit